                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/18974: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ireland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Dublin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-01-27">January 27, 1942</date>.<lb/>[Received January 27—1:10
                        p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5. Landing American troops port in Northern Ireland was broadcast yesterday from
                    London 9 p.m., from Dublin 10:10 p.m. This morning’s Dublin papers display news
                    briefly stating several thousand American combat troops with artillery landed
                    yesterday. Thus far no editorial comment.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
